{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a33bbe8cccfe52c5ec3cd9920f71e12359f54ca09d146518a98e032b3e8b89fe","digest":{"component_or_area":"completion verifier test harness","key_entities":["tests/external/test_completion_banking_behavior_0707.py","observed_upsert","tests/_bank_observer.py::make_observed_upsert","CriterionBank.upsert","evidence_sufficient","seeded","record_insufficient","src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py","src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py","test_completion_bank_observer_forwarding.py"],"problem_keywords":["signature drift","monkeypatch","keyword argument","test harness","type error"],"propositions":["The test monkeypatch stub observed_upsert() has a narrower signature than the real CriterionBank.upsert(), missing keyword-only parameters evidence_sufficient and seeded that production now passes.","When the bedrock arm's verify_completion workflow hits the bounded-fallback path (record_insufficient), it calls upsert(..., evidence_sufficient=False), causing the narrow stub to raise TypeError.","The anthropic and openai arms avoided the fallback path by gathering sufficient evidence, so the test passed on those arms despite the signature mismatch.","The fix threads all keyword arguments through the test stub via **kwargs to preserve evidence_sufficient, seeded, and future parameters unchanged to the real upsert."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787452432594461001,"uuid":"71caf9b7-adf8-4789-958e-be2e79ea9a02"}